 ## Overview
-Cutaways and Ghosting are illustrative volume rendering techniques that selectively suppress or reduce the opacity of occluding background structures to reveal a primary object of interest (Selection) [S1][S2, book]. Unlike standard transparency which blends all data, this method employs a three-object logical model (Selection, Ghost, Background) to create "magic views" that aid mental reconstruction of spatial relationships [S1][S2, book]. It sets itself apart from siblings like [Feature Halos](799-feature-halos.md) by explicitly managing occlusion through opacity reduction or removal rather than edge enhancement, and from [Context-Preserving Volume Rendering](801-context-preserving-volume-rendering.md) by allowing full suppression (cutaway) rather than just context preservation.
